edit — a file, in a real editor component.

The type declares its STATIC verbs only. `Save` is not among them: it is
emca's DYNAMIC verb, emitted while the buffer is dirty and withdrawn when it
is clean, because its appearance IS the dirty indicator (acme.c:383, with
acme's Put translated to the era's word).

Undo and Redo are here and nowhere else. Undo is available exactly where
every operation a window offers stays in a buffer emca holds — a killed
process does not come back, and a deleted file does not.
